\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The morning after the night before
\f1\b0\fs24 \

\f0\b\fs36 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 The debut party for Richard I was the biggest and most successful event the any Elvis had ever experienced. Dancing and drinking did not cease until well after the puny rays of sunrise. It was not noticed for a considerable time that some, in fact, most of the Elvi were feeling very unwell and seemed to be getting worse. The symptoms escalated quickly with some vomiting and shitting blood, while leaving others writhing on the ground with cold sweats and convulsions.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93This is not possible, your Elvisness.\'94 Professor Hermann entreated the H.E. and cabinet. \'93My virus should protect all Elvi from any biological pathogens. I don\'92t understand what is happening.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93What of poisons, non-biological agents?\'94 The Health Minister inquired. \'93Radiation?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93They should be protected from most poisons, even cyanide should not bother them.\'94 Professor Hermann assured them. \'93No blood work has come back yet, so I do not know what is harming them, or in what manner a poison may have been introduced. If we are talking poison, we are talking a mass poisoning at a single event.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Well it seems obvious it happened last night at Richard\'92s debut.\'94 The High Elvis concluded. \'93What some of us seem unaffected is a bit of a mystery, but I am sure we can find out. Are any of my brothers of sisters critical?\'94 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93No, not yet.\'94 Replied the Health Minister. \'93Some are gravely ill, but are still breathing on their own.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Well I think we will act on the assumption that we have all been poisoned, somehow.\'94 H.E. decided. \'93I want all of the caterers and their Dawks interviewed. I want samples of everything that was consumed last night. I want every surface of the stadium swabbed and tested for poisons. I want every clue followed up. I want this conundrum solved yesterday!\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf0  - - -
\f1 \

\f2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The Director of Proactive Euthenasia and Pre-emptive Reprocity, Damien Hardman was sitting at his desk, contemplating the previous night\'92s operation. They knew sending in Haloren Smythe would be the distraction they needed to pull off the master-plan. Having infiltrated the Dawks some months prior, the directorate was able to send hundreds of undercover operatives into the very heart of enemy territory and deliver some justice. The most difficult part of the operation was activating so many operatives and poisoning over 100,000 bottles of water at such short notice. Once delivered, the Dawk operative just had to hand it out.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Remember to stay hydrated.\'94 He giggled under his breath just as the giant double doors of his office burst open. \'93Mr CEO, very happy to see you.\'94 From the look on the CDO\'92s face the feel was not mutual.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93What happened last night?\'94 The CEO demanded. \'93I didn\'92t think any of them would even walk out of the stadium. I\'92ve got a few reports that some of them are sick, but we gave them enough poison to kill off the planet. How are any still alive?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93I cannot answer that, but all of the research showed the dosage should have been more that enough. They should be bleeding from every orifice by now.\'94 Damien assured.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93I don\'92t just want them bleeding, I want them dead.\'94  The CEO took a long breath. \'93I want them all dead!\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Okay, if they are near to death or just sick, they are vulnerable.\'94 Damien scratched his head, not knowing whether he should make the suggestion. \'93And I can send in troops to finish them off.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Yes, I don\'92t care how messy it is, this has to end.\'94 The CEO would not be happy until the operation was completed. \'93Just one thing, Eloise Shakti\'92s grandson, Richard, has an Elvis security team, if they get in the way make sure you kill him along with the rest. You have seen the reports from your undercover Dawks. The child was named Richard I of the Elvi. For the love of money! The crowning of a King under my watch? Intolerable.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93That\'92s her grandson?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93There is some evidence to suggest that Alexander Shakti is not the father.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93But still, are you sure you want to cross her?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93It cannot be avoided.\'94 
\f3\i I won\'92t be crossing her, you will. 
\f1\i0 \

\f2 \
\'93I understand.\'94 Damien nodded and smiled, hiding his true reaction to this insane plan. Damien knew where true power lay and fucking with Eloise is not something he was prepared to do. He would not fair any better than Haloran Smythe. He would rather use himself as a human shield to protect that kid if it meant keeping Eloise on-side. \'93His fate is sealed.\'94 Of course he was not talking of Richard-Dawkins Jacobson Shakti. This was the moment Damien and the CEO parted ways. 
\f3\i Fuck him, Damien thought.
\f1\i0 \

\f2 \
\'93I will leave you to your planning, but I suggest you get onto this as soon as possible. This matter must be finalised within 72 hours.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Why 72 hrs?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Because I fucking said so.\'94 And the CEO was gone.
\f1 \

\f2 \
Damien buzzed his secretary. \'93Get Eloise Shakti on a secure line for me, Janine.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
Within a minute he was looking at a hologram of the richest and most powerful person in the primary trade dominion. Like every other kid, he was brought up on the amazing stories of how she smashed her way through the glass ceiling and landed on top of the pile. She was a walking metaphor for power and grace. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93What does a low grade public servant want with me?\'94 She asked with indignation.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93I\'92m the Director of Proactive Euthanasia and Pre-emptive Reciprocity!\'94 He could not help but take the bait.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Exactly.\'94 She had to put him in his place. She figured this call had something to do with the raid on her house and she wasn\'92t going to take any shit.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Ma\'92am I think I have reached an ethical impasse, a problem that I cannot resolve without the assistance and protection of a person of your stature.\'94 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Go on.\'94 She liked it when others acknowledged her power.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93The CEO has asked me, no sorry, ordered me to execute your grandson.\'94 He decided on no euphemisms.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Oh, really? Tell me more Mr Hardman.\'94 Her mind went into overdrive.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf0  
\f4\b - - -
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \'93It was in the bottled water, some sort of synthetic ebola-like poison. Anyone who drank the bottled water will be very unwell.\'94 Professor Hermann reported to cabinet that same afternoon. \'93It\'92s safe to say your army of Dawks have been compromised.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93We cannot trust any of them\'94 The High Elvis concluded. \'93We are on our own. Will our Elvi survive?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93I have never seen any agent so diabolical. Any average human or clone for that matter, would die within hours of ingestion. Our Elvi are being afforded protection by the Hybrid T-virus (\cf2 find the actual name of the virus)\cf0  and I am confident they can fight it off.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93This has left the us vulnerable and we must be given the time to regroup. We will not be able to repel any aggression with so many layed-low.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Well, what if we do die?\'94 Cracker, The Great Teacher, said.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93What do you mean?\'94 The High Elvis replied angrily. \'93 If we die, all is lost.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93I mean, what if we let it be known the Elvi are dying of some mystery illness? A cloning error, perhaps.\'94 The Great Teacher was met with blank looks. \'93They won\'92t need to finish us off if they think they have succeeded. Hopefully, by the time the PTD find out it was bullshit, the Elvi will have recovered.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Does any member of the cabinet have any better ideas?\'94 It was the High Elvis\'92 turn to be met with blank stares. \'93No? Let it be known that the Elvi are dying out, but first, let our Elvi brothers and sisters know of this ruse. We don\'92t need them to freak-out.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93We will have to make it look good. We will need mourning and wailing in the streets and funerals, plenty of funerals.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93No, mass graves and funeral pyres.\'94 The High Elvis had spoken.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf0  - - -
\f1 \

\f2 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'91It looks like the poison is working Mr CEO.\'94 Damien Hardman was glad to announce when he called to give an update. \'93According to the latest intelligence the poison has taken out thousands already. There are pyres burning all through The Quarter and they keep piling bodies on. I\'92ve seen the surveillance vid.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Keep an eye on it, I want a 100% termination rate.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93What about Richard I?\'94 Damien chuckled silently to himself.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93He is still on my hit list.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Just to be perfectly clear, you want me to assassinate Eloise Shakti\'92s grandson.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93The sooner the better.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Thank you sir, the wheels are in motion.\'94 Director Hardman terminated the link. He looked across his desk and said, \'93Enough proof for you?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Yes, you have proved your worth.\'94 said Eloise Shakti, seated in a chair on the opposite side of the desk. \'93I will not forget this, Mr Hardman.\'94 
\f1 \

